11. Convert Python Dictionary to JSON String

Program: Write a Python program using the json module that creates a Python dictionary containing employee details, converts it to a JSON string, and displays the result.

Methods Covered:

json.dumps()

12. Convert JSON String to Python Dictionary

Program: Write a Python program using the json module that reads a JSON string containing employee information, converts it into a Python dictionary, and displays all key-value pairs.

Methods Covered:

json.loads()

13. Write JSON Data to a File

Program: Write a Python program using the json module that stores student information in a dictionary and writes the data to a file named student.json.

Methods Covered:

json.dump()

14. Read JSON Data from a File

Program: Write a Python program using the json module that reads data from student.json and displays all information.

Methods Covered:

json.load()

15. Pretty Print JSON Data

Program: Write a Python program using the json module that converts a Python dictionary into a neatly formatted JSON string with indentation and displays it.

Methods Covered:

json.dumps()
indent

16. Check Whether a Key Exists in JSON

Program: Write a Python program using the json module that reads a JSON object containing employee information, checks whether the key salary exists, and prints an appropriate message.

Methods Covered:

json.loads()
in operator

17. Add a New Key to JSON Data

Program: Write a Python program using the json module that reads employee data from employee.json, adds a new key named department, saves the file, and displays a success message.

Methods Covered:

json.load()
json.dump()
dictionary assignment

18. Delete a Key from JSON Data

Program: Write a Python program using the json module that reads employee data from employee.json, removes the key age, saves the updated file, and displays a confirmation message.

Methods Covered:

json.load()
del
json.dump()

19. Update an Existing Value in JSON

Program: Write a Python program using the json module that reads employee information from employee.json, changes the value of the city key to Bengaluru, saves the file, and prints a success message.

Methods Covered:

json.load()
json.dump()
dictionary assignment

20. Display All Keys and Values in JSON

Program: Write a Python program using the json module that reads employee data from employee.json and displays all keys and values in the format key : value.

Methods Covered:

json.load()
dictionary.items()


These questions follow the same beginner-friendly style as your ConfigParser module questions and focus on the core JSON methods: dumps(), loads(), dump(), load(), along with common operations such as add, update, delete, search, and display.
